  "prostate": {
    "label": "Prostate Cancer Risk",
    "shipped": false,
    "withdrawn_reason": "Held-out test AUC 0.786, 95% CI 0.505 to 0.99. The lower bound sits on chance, so the panel cannot be shown to work. Specificity is 0.571 with a CI of 0.167 to 1.0, an interval so wide it carries no information, because the test split is 20 records. The ensemble also fails to beat plain logistic regression (0.769) by any meaningful margin. 97 records and two usable screening features cannot support a clinical claim, so this panel is trained and measured but not served.",
    "cohort_design": "Case-control and post-prostatectomy. Gleason grade comes from the surgical specimen, not from screening."
  }
